['How to plan '.$b['intent'].' in '.$d,"A useful $kw starts with realistic travel time. Choose the experiences that matter most, group nearby places and keep one flexible period for weather, traffic or rest. {$b['highlights']} are natural anchors, but current opening hours, entry rules and local conditions should be confirmed before departure. Avoid building a schedule from map estimates alone; parking, queues and narrow heritage streets can change the pace of a day."],
['Suggested route and daily pacing',"Begin outdoor sightseeing early, use the middle of the day for lunch, museums or hotel rest, and reserve a clear late afternoon for markets, waterfronts or viewpoints. For a short visit, select one compact sightseeing zone each day. For a longer trip, add a nearby excursion without changing hotels unnecessarily. Families, senior travellers and young children need extra breaks, while photographers may prefer sunrise and sunset windows."],
['Best season and what to pack',"October to March usually offers easier sightseeing across much of North India, while monsoon travel can bring greener landscapes and occasional disruption. Summer requires early starts, hydration and air-conditioned breaks. Pack comfortable shoes, sun protection, identity documents, prescribed medicines and a light layer for cool evenings. Always check the short-range forecast because seasonal averages cannot predict conditions on your exact dates."],
['Transport and local movement',"Select transport according to group size, luggage and route. Walking is often fastest inside old quarters; registered autos or cabs suit short transfers; a reserved vehicle helps with outstation stops. Confirm pickup points, waiting charges, tolls, parking and driver allowance in writing. For self-drive plans, review licence, deposit, insurance, fuel and damage policies carefully. Never continue with a tired driver or an unsafe vehicle."],
['Where to stay',"Choose an area based on sightseeing access, station or airport transfers, parking, lift availability and evening plans. A heritage-core stay may offer atmosphere but can involve stairs and narrow lanes. Modern districts may be easier for vehicles and families. Check recent verified reviews, the exact map position, taxes, meal inclusions, cancellation rules and room configuration before payment. Retain written confirmation and a valid invoice."],
['Food, shopping and local culture',"Use busy, established food outlets and communicate allergies or dietary needs clearly. Try regional dishes gradually on long travel days. At markets, compare quality, ask before photographing people and collect bills for valuable purchases. Dress respectfully at religious places and follow local rules for shoes, cameras and ceremonies. Supporting licensed guides, local drivers, artisans and responsible family-run businesses keeps more tourism value in the destination."],
['Budget and booking checklist',"Build the budget from accommodation, intercity travel, local transport, meals, tickets, guides, activities, taxes and a contingency. Online prices change, so treat estimates as ranges rather than guarantees. Before booking, verify operator identity, itinerary, hotel category, cancellation terms and inclusions. Avoid transferring money only on the basis of social-media images. A written quotation should state passenger count, travel dates, vehicle type and exclusions."],
['Common planning mistakes to avoid',"Trying to cover too many distant attractions, booking non-refundable services too early and ignoring transfer buffers are common problems. Another mistake is choosing only the lowest quotation without comparing vehicle quality, hotel location or service scope. Keep digital and offline copies of bookings, share the itinerary with a trusted contact and protect personal information. Attraction prices, regulations and road conditions can change, so reconfirm close to travel."],
